{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: BR-3, two workers for the Scope test project. Head 76c5d39ee51383b5a851a586149af51838e9fcb9, tree b2d5ca4c330e770651633066e836803334a2e088, branch request/br3-worker-parallelism-20261026: twelve commits on d36773b3, twelve paths, all twelve named by the artifacts. Review request 2ba0f8d1, checker promise 62a778b0, request 50695e48 (builder promise 267ac638).\n\nRead order: the primary note at the head in full; request 50695e48; the builder's isolation question 0db80e82 and planner ruling 29be9662; the configuration and script diff; the Lending test and stand-in diff, split at V2 (cbb08aff); docs/testing.md; then the evidence and the composition with Main.\n\nAcceptance (\"The project runs with two or more workers; one measurement run and one ordinary gate pass, with phase times before and after\"): met. packages/scope/vitest.worker.config.ts sets maxWorkers 2 with isolate false. Under ruling cf0328ba one ordinary gate, G3 at 9c2d5f4b, is both the validation and the after measurement, and it passed. The before figures are BR-9's passing gate on one worker. Native phase wall was 1,310.25 s before and 753.64 s after; whole gate wall was 1,431.83 s before and 882.24 s after. These are uncontrolled observations on different trees, loads and cache states, and the note rightly claims no ratio.\n\nRuling 29be9662. I checked its four conditions at the head:\n1. Scope of change. From V2 (cbb08aff) to the accepted proposal bd9d4dec, the only source changes are the native project inventory (the new vitest.lending.config.ts, vitest.config.ts, the exclude in vitest.worker.config.ts, vitest.projects.mjs), the phase-selection and summary witnesses (test-phases, test-summary and its test), docs/testing.md, and one diagnostic suffix on the first assertion in lending.test.ts. No production bytes change anywhere on the branch. The bounded read restart in the stand-in and the moved return came earlier, in e29acab4, before V2. Question 0db80e82 describes that repair, so the ruling accepted it as part of the proposal's base.\n2. Order. The owning checks ran once at bd9d4dec after BR-10's gate closed (d4ecdfd4, 13:41). G3 started at 13:42 (f5437567) and passed at 13:57 (6e842591). The head differs from G3's checkpoint only in the note, the removal of six branch-only manifests and the new delivery manifest. None of those six manifests exists on Main, so the documents-only rule applies and no second gate is owed.\n3. Record. The note keeps V1 (eceeb5e9) and V2 (cbb08aff) as separate failed outcomes with their analyses, explains the isolation, and names BR-4 (15b0f8ab, open) as owner of the unknown cross-file cause and the lending.test.ts:237 record.\n4. Stop rule: not triggered, because G3 passed.\n\nTest changes. I read them as the riskiest part of the head.\n- The stand-in now makes at most two complete read attempts. Before it compares heads, it validates each source on its own through the unchanged strict projector. Any malformed, refused, incomplete or transport error still propagates at once. Only a mismatch between source heads and the history head on the first attempt starts the one restart. After that, the full strict projector decides, so a second mismatch still refuses.\n- The story now performs the passer-by's return and the drain inside the first item read, so every run exercises the restart. The paired control shows the guard is needed: with only the restart disabled, the first look fails with status \"behind\" through the intended AssertionError, and the restored helper is byte-identical.\n- No assertion is removed or loosened. The first look must still be current with member actions only, the item must be available with no borrower, and the second look must show the same three things. The earlier settle before the projection now runs inside the read, after the return. The diagnostic labels are a fixed set of at most three, and the original errors are rethrown unchanged.\n\nSelection. Lending is excluded from the two-worker project and selected only by scope-lending. The root scope project replaces include but not exclude, so the root also selects the story once. G3's native total of 782 equals BR-10's gate on Main, so no native file was dropped or run twice. I ran node --test scripts/test-phases.test.mjs scripts/test-summary.test.mjs at the head in the builder's worktree: 4 passed, and the worktree stayed clean.\n\nComposition. The head sits on d36773b3, not on Main 986c7120. git merge-tree merges it onto 986c7120 with no conflict, and the result differs from the head only in BR-9's three paths: a plain CLI configuration test and its note and manifest. They do not touch the native projects, the Lending story or the test scripts. The head's paths are also disjoint from the approved BR-10 head 8dc9edc2. No merged-tree gate is claimed or owed.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One more project with its own runtime and a fixed group order is the smallest isolation, and the partition guard in vitest.projects.mjs now checks the order for any number of native projects. Each worker owns its Miniflare, archive clocks and fixtures, the clone server uses separate directories and random sessions, and captured packets are immutable, so the two workers share no mutable state that the head knows of.\n\nSecurity: no change to production code, authority, settings, dependencies or deployment. The restart lives only in a test stand-in, and the strict projector still guards the production path.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. The source change is small and the new configuration file is 15 lines. The note (21,362 bytes) and the 181-file manifest are heavy for a configuration change, but both are correct.\n\nLimits for the planner (nonblocking):\n1. With Lending in its own runtime, the gate no longer runs that story alongside other files, so the cross-file interaction behind V1 and V2 is no longer exercised. BR-4 owns the cause; it should say whether the story returns to the shared project once the cause is known.\n2. The stand-in still refuses if the native head moves on both attempts. That fails closed and is visible.\n3. docs/testing.md is a documentation path. If the area-wide docs artifact 42e1aca1 blocked BR-10's landing (3eb885c5), it may block this landing too.\n\nEvidence, verified by me:\n- Manifest digest 288bbc2a… matches the request. All 181 files match their size and SHA-256 digest; nothing in /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-10-26-br3-worker-parallelism-delivery is writable (0 of 207 entries); all 180 SHA256SUMS lines pass.\n- g3/result.json (SHA-256 8fb9ad9a…, equal to the note) records head 9c2d5f4b, tree 4d697010, Main 986c7120 before and after, exit 0, and an empty status afterwards. g3/gate.log shows changed files 0, every step at exit 0, notes 0 warnings, kernel, Node, Counting, plain 2,835 passed and 1 skipped, and native 780 passed and 2 skipped.\n- The before figures come only from the pinned baseline-observations.json (525e8cb1…). The control, the diagnostic run, V1 and V2 are the builder's records; I read them and did not rerun them.\n- Commit subjects are 43 to 57 characters, and git diff --check is clean over the branch.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 76c5d39e / tree b2d5ca4c. The builder lands. No deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c972a74ca626468b01df155b5a7104d35582f278","binding":"assigned","head":"76c5d39ee51383b5a851a586149af51838e9fcb9","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:62a778b071742423301a83e55e51ee269f38fd8f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:267ac638c2881333993cfe810454475c8a9b5cdd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:62a778b071742423301a83e55e51ee269f38fd8f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}